    starter: { html: `<header>\n  <h1>Your Name</h1>\n  <p>B.Tech AI student</p>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <section id="about"><h2>About</h2><p>Write about yourself.</p></section>\n  <section id="skills"><h2>Skills</h2><ul><li>HTML</li></ul></section>\n</main>\n<footer></footer>`, css: `body { font-family: system-ui; margin: 0; }\n` },
    solution: { html: `<header class="hero">\n  <h1>Riya Verma</h1>\n  <p>B.Tech AI student · I build friendly websites</p>\n  <nav><a href="#about">About</a><a href="#skills">Skills</a><a href="#projects">Projects</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <section id="about"><h2>About</h2><p>I am a first-year student who loves turning ideas into web pages. Currently learning HTML, CSS and JavaScript.</p></section>\n  <section id="skills"><h2>Skills</h2>\n    <ul class="pills"><li>HTML5</li><li>CSS3</li><li>Flexbox</li><li>JavaScript</li><li>Git</li></ul>\n  </section>\n  <section id="projects"><h2>Projects</h2>\n    <div class="cards">\n      <article class="card"><h3>Calculator</h3><p>A working calculator with keyboard support.</p><a href="#">View code →</a></article>\n      <article class="card"><h3>To-do App</h3><p>Tasks saved in localStorage.</p><a href="#">View code →</a></article>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n</main>\n<footer id="contact"><p>Say hi: <a href="mailto:riya@example.com">riya@example.com</a></p></footer>`, css: `:root { --brand: #FF8A3D; --ink: #30343B; --soft: #FFF9EF; }\nbody { margin: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--ink); background: var(--soft); line-height: 1.6; }\n.hero { text-align: center; padding: 40px 16px 20px; background: #FFE3CF; }\n.hero h1 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem); }\nnav { display: flex; gap: 14px; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 10px; }\nnav a { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--brand); }\nsection { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; }\n.pills { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }\n.pills li { background: #DDF1FB; border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 99px; padding: 2px 12px; }\n.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }\n.card { background: #fff; border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink); }\nfooter { text-align: center; padding: 20px; }` },
    explanation: 'Semantic tags give the page a clear outline. The nav uses Flexbox with wrap so links never overflow on phones. Skills are a list (because they are a list!) styled as pills. Project cards use Grid with auto-fit + minmax, so the layout becomes one column on small screens without any media query. CSS variables keep colours consistent.',
