    steps: ['Create an article with image area, title, rating, prices and a button.', 'Make the card position: relative and pin a discount badge with absolute.', 'Show the old price with <del>.', 'Add a hover lift using transform and transition.'],
    starter: { html: `<article class="card">\n  <h3>Product name</h3>\n  <button>Add to cart</button>\n</article>`, css: `.card { width: 240px; }` },
    solution: { html: `<article class="card">\n  <span class="badge">-35%</span>\n  <div class="img">👟</div>\n  <h3>CloudRun Sneakers</h3>\n  <p class="rating" aria-label="Rated 4.5 out of 5">★★★★☆ <small>(1,204)</small></p>\n  <p class="price"><strong>₹1,949</strong> <del>₹2,999</del></p>\n  <button>Add to cart</button>\n</article>`, css: `body { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 90vh; background: #FFF9EF; font-family: system-ui; }\n.card { position: relative; width: 240px; padding: 14px; background: #fff; border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 16px; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #30343B; transition: transform .25s, box-shadow .25s; }\n.card:hover { transform: translateY(-6px); box-shadow: 6px 10px 0 #30343B; }\n.badge { position: absolute; top: -12px; left: -12px; background: #F48FB1; border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 99px; padding: 4px 10px; font-weight: 800; transform: rotate(-8deg); }\n.img { height: 140px; display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 72px; background: #DDF1FB; border-radius: 12px; }\nh3 { margin: 10px 0 2px; }\n.rating { color: #E0A800; margin: 0; }\n.price strong { font-size: 1.3rem; } .price del { color: #8a8f98; }\nbutton { width: 100%; padding: 10px; border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 10px; background: #FFD45C; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; transition: transform .1s; }\nbutton:active { transform: scale(.96); }` },
    explanation: 'The badge uses absolute positioning relative to the card (which is relative). Negative top/left let it hang over the corner. transform-based hover effects are smooth because they do not trigger layout. The rating has an aria-label so screen readers do not read out "black star black star…".',
