    steps: ['Keep tasks in an array of objects { id, text, done } — this is your state.', 'Write render() that rebuilds the list from the array.', 'Add tasks on form submit; toggle and delete with event delegation.', 'Save the array to localStorage as JSON after every change; load it on start.'],
    starter: { html: `<form id="f"><input id="t"><button>Add</button></form>\n<ul id="list"></ul>`, css: ``, js: `let tasks = [];\nfunction render() {\n  // build the list here\n}` },
    solution: { html: `<main class="todo">\n  <h2>My Tasks</h2>\n  <form id="f"><input id="t" placeholder="What do you need to do?" aria-label="New task" required><button>Add</button></form>\n  <ul id="list"></ul>\n  <p id="left"></p>\n</main>`, css: `body { font-family: system-ui; background: #FFF9EF; }\n.todo { max-width: 380px; margin: 20px auto; }\nform { display: flex; gap: 6px; }\ninput { flex: 1; padding: 8px; border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 8px; }\nbutton { border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 8px; background: #78C86A; font-weight: 700; padding: 0 12px; cursor: pointer; }\nul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }\nli { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 8px; margin: 6px 0; background: #fff; border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 10px; }\nli span { flex: 1; cursor: pointer; }\nli.done span { text-decoration: line-through; opacity: .55; }\nli .del { background: #F48FB1; }`, js: `const KEY = "codeplay-todos";\nlet tasks = load();\n\nfunction load() {\n  try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY)) || []; } catch { return []; }\n}\nfunction save() {\n  try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(tasks)); } catch { /* sandbox may block storage */ }\n}\nfunction render() {\n  const list = document.getElementById("list");\n  list.innerHTML = "";\n  tasks.forEach((t) => {\n    const li = document.createElement("li");\n    li.dataset.id = t.id;\n    li.className = t.done ? "done" : "";\n    const span = document.createElement("span");\n    span.textContent = t.text;\n    const del = document.createElement("button");\n    del.textContent = "✕"; del.className = "del"; del.setAttribute("aria-label", "Delete " + t.text);\n    li.append(span, del);\n    list.append(li);\n  });\n  const left = tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length;\n  document.getElementById("left").textContent = left + " task(s) left";\n  save();\n}\n\ndocument.getElementById("f").addEventListener("submit", (e) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const input = document.getElementById("t");\n  tasks.push({ id: Date.now(), text: input.value.trim(), done: false });\n  input.value = "";\n  render();\n});\n\ndocument.getElementById("list").addEventListener("click", (e) => {\n  const id = Number(e.target.closest("li")?.dataset.id);\n  if (e.target.classList.contains("del")) tasks = tasks.filter((t) => t.id !== id);\n  else if (e.target.tagName === "SPAN") tasks = tasks.map((t) => (t.id === id ? { ...t, done: !t.done } : t));\n  render();\n});\n\nrender();` },
    explanation: 'The tasks array is the single source of truth (state); the DOM is always rebuilt from it by render(). This "state → render" pattern is exactly how React works. Event delegation means new items work without new listeners. textContent (not innerHTML) protects against users typing HTML. JSON turns the array into a string for localStorage.',
    challenges: ['Add filters: All / Active / Done.', 'Allow editing a task on double-click.'],
