    id: 'clock', title: 'Digital Clock', level: 'Beginner', tracks: ['html', 'css', 'js'],
    objective: 'Show the current time and date, updating every second, with a 12/24-hour toggle.',
    concepts: ['js-async', 'js-strings-math', 'js-dom'],
    steps: ['Create elements for time and date.', 'Write update() that reads new Date() and formats hours, minutes, seconds with padStart.', 'Call it every second with setInterval.', 'Add a button to switch between 12 and 24-hour format.'],
    starter: { html: `<div id="time">00:00:00</div>`, css: ``, js: `function update() {\n  const now = new Date();\n}\n` },
    solution: { html: `<div class="clock">\n  <div id="time">--:--:--</div>\n  <div id="date"></div>\n  <button id="fmt">Switch to 12-hour</button>\n</div>`, css: `body { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 95vh; margin: 0; background: #30343B; font-family: system-ui; }\n.clock { text-align: center; color: #FFF9EF; }\n#time { font: 700 clamp(2.5rem, 12vw, 5rem) ui-monospace, monospace; color: #FFD45C; letter-spacing: 2px; }\n#date { margin: 6px 0 14px; opacity: .8; }\nbutton { padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 99px; border: 2px solid #FFF9EF; background: transparent; color: #FFF9EF; cursor: pointer; }`, js: `let use12 = false;\nconst pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, "0");\n\nfunction update() {\n  const now = new Date();\n  let h = now.getHours();\n  let suffix = "";\n  if (use12) { suffix = h >= 12 ? " PM" : " AM"; h = h % 12 || 12; }\n  document.getElementById("time").textContent = pad(h) + ":" + pad(now.getMinutes()) + ":" + pad(now.getSeconds()) + suffix;\n  document.getElementById("date").textContent = now.toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { weekday: "long", day: "numeric", month: "long", year: "numeric" });\n}\n\ndocument.getElementById("fmt").addEventListener("click", (e) => {\n  use12 = !use12;\n  e.target.textContent = use12 ? "Switch to 24-hour" : "Switch to 12-hour";\n  update();\n});\n\nupdate();\nsetInterval(update, 1000);` },
    explanation: 'setInterval calls update() every 1000ms. padStart(2, "0") turns 7 into "07". h % 12 || 12 converts 0 and 12 to 12 for the 12-hour clock (because 0 is falsy, || picks 12). toLocaleDateString formats the date in Indian English.',
    challenges: ['Add a stopwatch with start/stop/reset.', 'Show a greeting: Good morning / afternoon / evening.'],
