    starter: { html: `<div class="gallery"></div>`, css: ``, js: `` },
    solution: { html: `<div class="gallery">\n  <button class="ph wide" style="--c:#FF8A3D">Campus</button>\n  <button class="ph" style="--c:#55B9E8">Library</button>\n  <button class="ph" style="--c:#78C86A">Garden</button>\n  <button class="ph" style="--c:#FFD45C">Fest</button>\n  <button class="ph" style="--c:#F48FB1">Lab</button>\n  <button class="ph" style="--c:#9BD5F0">Sports</button>\n</div>\n<div class="lightbox" id="lb" hidden><div class="big" id="big"></div><p>Click anywhere or press Esc to close</p></div>`, css: `body { font-family: system-ui; margin: 12px; }\n.gallery { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(120px, 1fr)); gap: 8px; }\n.ph { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; background: var(--c); border: 2px solid #30343B; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 700; cursor: zoom-in; transition: transform .2s; }\n.ph:hover { transform: scale(1.03); }\n.wide { grid-column: span 2; aspect-ratio: auto; }\n.lightbox { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 100; background: rgba(48,52,59,.85); display: grid; place-items: center; color: #fff; }\n.lightbox[hidden] { display: none; }\n.big { width: min(80vw, 520px); aspect-ratio: 4/3; border-radius: 14px; border: 3px solid #fff; display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #30343B; }`, js: `const lb = document.getElementById("lb");\nconst big = document.getElementById("big");\ndocument.querySelector(".gallery").addEventListener("click", (e) => {\n  const ph = e.target.closest(".ph");\n  if (!ph) return;\n  big.textContent = ph.textContent;\n  big.style.background = getComputedStyle(ph).getPropertyValue("--c");\n  lb.hidden = false;\n});\nlb.addEventListener("click", () => (lb.hidden = true));\ndocument.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => { if (e.key === "Escape") lb.hidden = true; });` },
    explanation: 'auto-fill + minmax makes as many 120px+ columns as fit. The lightbox is position: fixed with inset: 0 (top/right/bottom/left 0) and a high z-index so it covers everything. The hidden attribute plus a CSS rule controls visibility. Buttons are used for photos so they are keyboard-accessible.',
